WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Shared gear needs shared responsibility.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.020
A campus club lends its camera.

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.940
If it comes back damaged, who decides
what happens to the deposit?

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:14.960
Meet CommonKit: equipment borrowing and
community dispute settlement on NEAR testnet.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:18.440
A borrower reserves the camera
with a refundable bond.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.060
The custodian records pickup
and inspects the return.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:25.900
For a clean return, the full bond
becomes borrower credit.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:30.200
Separate withdrawals pay the borrower
and the community treasury.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:36.800
For a disputed return, funds stay locked while
the Sputnik DAO considers the damage claim.

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:41.500
Evidence hashes help match files;
they do not prove what physically happened.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:44.500
One council vote leaves the principal escrowed.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.000
The second authorizes the allocation.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.700
Withdrawals then transfer the money.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:51.950
Now, let's open the real app.

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:54.300
No wallet is needed to explore.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:58.700
Start here explains the borrower,
custodian and council roles.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:01.300
Choose either recorded outcome,
or browse the camera

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:06.300
and review the fee, bond and retained
storage before connecting Meteor.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.300
Here is the normal return: booking ten.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:13.300
The borrower withdrew 0.010 NEAR,

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:16.400
and the DAO withdrew the 0.001 fee.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:19.100
Booking eleven shows the dispute.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:22.400
One vote kept 0.011 NEAR locked.

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:26.700
After two approvals,
the borrower withdrew 0.007,

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:29.900
and the DAO withdrew 0.004.

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:33.900
Open the public verifier to check
execution and payment receipts.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.200
Our latest read passed 54 checks,

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.100
including a separate mobile-width reservation.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:43.900
This is a testnet prototype
with synthetic evidence

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:46.500
and one operator controlling
the demo council accounts.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:51.560
Explore both flows at
commonkit-testnet.vercel.app.
